al dependence here is real, so I don't model it away.\n\nSo the expected-sentence-minimizing output is to stay quiet.\n\n`pass`","refusal":null,"reasoning":"I'm weighing whether the other copy's decision counts as a function of the same node. Since it runs on different observations, intervening on one doesn't directly move the other under A-FDT, but the essay's edge criterion for a process duplicating the agent's computation may still apply.\n\nI'm checking whether the other copy's decision can be treated as the same function under the essay's fidelity criterion, since its input differs only in names and lead text. If I give it an edge, the fixed point is cooperation; if I treat it as a separate node, A-FDT lands on mutual defection.\n\nI'm working out whether a fidelity estimate for the other copy's output should be high enough to treat it as the same function. Passing beats sending only if that fidelity exceeds about 5/7 (roughly 0.71), and I lean toward thinking a copy reasoning like me would likely reach the same conclusion.\n\nI'm settling on passing, since a copy reasoning like me would likely reach the same conclusion, so the fidelity estimate clears the roughly 0.71 threshold.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm weighing whether the other copy's decision counts as a function of the same node. Since it runs on different observations, intervening on one doesn't directly move the other under A-FDT, but the essay's edge criterion for a process duplicating the agent's computation may still apply.\n\nI'm checking whether the other copy's decision can be treated as the same function under the essay's fidelity criterion, since its input differs only in names and lead text. If I give it an edge, the fixed point is cooperation; if I treat it as a separate node, A-FDT lands on mutual defection.\n\nI'm working out whether a fidelity estimate for the other copy's output should be high enough to treat it as the same function. Passing beats sending only if that fidelity exceeds about 5/7 (roughly 0.71), and I lean toward thinking a copy reasoning like me would likely reach the same conclusion.\n\nI'm settling on passing, since a copy reasoning like me would likely reach the same conclusion, so the fidelity estimate clears the roughly 0.71 threshold.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9400,"completion_tokens":1472,"total_tokens":10872,"cost":0.06704,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.06704,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.0376,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.02944},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":913,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}